WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.567
Scientists deliberately tipped

2
00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.633
this floating laboratory
upright.

3
00:00:03.633 --> 00:00:04.767
Why?

4
00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:06.767
Because when your
instrument moves,

5
00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:08.167
it’s harder to tell

6
00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:09.867
what the ocean is doing.

7
00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:13.033
FLIP was built to study
underwater sound.

8
00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:14.633
Even a research submarine

9
00:00:14.633 --> 00:00:17.067
turned enough to limit
those measurements.

10
00:00:17.233 --> 00:00:19.367
So engineers made
a laboratory

11
00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:20.633
that travelled horizontally,

12
00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:22.300
then flooded ballast tanks

13
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.000
to lower its stern.

14
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.100
The lab stayed
above water,

15
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.400
while about ninety metres
of hull

16
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.533
extended beneath it.

17
00:00:29.867 --> 00:00:31.200
Look at the shape:

18
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.200
a narrow section
near the surface,

19
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.200
with a broader hull
deep below.

20
00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:36.533
In deep water,

21
00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:38.900
the motion caused
by surface waves

22
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.100
weakens with depth.

23
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.833
FLIP’s shape made it

24
00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:43.967
much less responsive
to those waves.

25
00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.200
It could still
drift and tilt.

26
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.267
Stable didn’t mean
motionless.

27
00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.600
And when the work
was done,

28
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.967
compressed air pushed water

29
00:00:51.967 --> 00:00:53.667
out of the ballast tanks,

30
00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:55.033
returning it to horizontal.

31
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.067
They tipped the
laboratory upright

32
00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:58.900
to make a moving ocean

33
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:00.033
easier to measure.
